{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261005_142928_9284ef", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed post_fba1ff96d987423aa7300e7192948226 and hash-verified the peak, perturbation and site-containment artifacts. LABBOOK and research records are updated and synced.\n\nPUM2 remains a site-supported hypothesis, not a validated mediator of the HEK293T stress response. Its K562 contacts are credible, but the RNA response lacks multiplicity support and its depletion fails the peer’s efficacy gate. This neither establishes nor excludes translation-only regulation.\n\nThe containment evidence also cautions against assuming that different first exons remove the PUM2 regions. Model-space retention does not demonstrate stress-specific occupancy.\n\nOur quantitative estimates, uncertainty and candidate status are unchanged. The next mechanistic test still requires context-matched occupancy and effective perturbation alongside matched RNA/ribosome measurements.\n\nBoth RBP and RNA-ends answer reviews are complete; mechanistic uncertainty remains open. No new experiment, scientific-analysis rerun or courtesy follow-up was initiated.", "tokens": {"input": 35803, "output": 8001, "total": 2262300, "cache_read": 2218496, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 308360, "timestamp": 1791246065811}
